{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1794213559, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.008497, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m$ rtp_gen: 30 s of G.711 with 3% loss, 20 ms jitter, reordering, duplicates, sequence wraparound\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.016852, "o", "rtp_gen --out demo.pcap --duration 30 --seed 42 --loss 0.03 --jitter-ms 20 --jitter-dist normal --reorder 0.01 --duplicate 0.01 --wrap\r\n"]
[1.030008, "o", "wrote /tmp/tmp.cxLLdoLWpe/demo.pcap (1478 packets in capture) and /tmp/tmp.cxLLdoLWpe/demo.pcap.truth\r\n"]
[1.031662, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m$ cat demo.pcap.truth   # what the generator actually did (ground truth)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.037524, "o", "packets_sent=1500\r\npackets_dropped=31\r\npackets_duplicated=9\r\npackets_reordered=13\r\n"]
[4.044029, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m$ rtp_scope demo.pcap   # what the analyzer measured\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.056823, "o", "rtp-scope: /tmp/tmp.cxLLdoLWpe/demo.pcap\r\n  link type          : Ethernet (1), microsecond timestamps\r\n  frames in capture  : 1478\r\n  RTP / RTCP         : 1478 / 0\r\n  non-RTP UDP        : 0\r\n  non-IPv4 / non-UDP : 0 / 0\r\n  IPv4 fragments     : 0 (skipped)\r\n  malformed          : 0 (network 0, rtp 0)\r\n\r\nstreams: 1\r\n\r\n #  source                destination           SSRC       PT         packets    dur(s)      kbps\r\n 0  10.0.0.1:5004         10.0.0.2:5004         0x11223344 0 PCMU        1478    30.005     67.78\r\n\r\n #  ext.highest  expected   lost   loss%   dup   ooo jitter(ts) jitter(ms)\r\n 0        66999      1500     31    2.07     9    13      94.54     11.817\r\n\r\n  dup = duplicate packets, ooo = out-of-order packets, jitter per RFC 3550 6.4.1\r\n"]
[8.100107, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m$ rtp_scope --simulate demo.pcap   # jitter-buffer strategies\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.115585, "o", "jitter-buffer simulation, stream #0 (10.0.0.1:5004 -> 10.0.0.2:5004, SSRC 0x11223344, 8000 Hz)\r\n  expected 1500 packets; 31 never arrived (lost in the network)\r\n\r\n strategy           played   late   lost  late+lost %  avg lat (ms)  max lat (ms)\r\n fixed-60ms           1469      0     31         2.07         54.01         85.25\r\n adaptive-k4          1461      8     31         2.60         39.09         70.58\r\n\r\n  late = arrived after its playout time (discarded); latency = time a played packet\r\n  waits in the buffer. Playout is scheduled relative to the first packet that arrived.\r\n"]
